WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.199 --> 00:00:03.539
(airplane taking off)

00:00:03.539 --> 00:00:05.995
- For those who can't afford to travel,

00:00:05.995 --> 00:00:08.595
what is the best way to expand your mind?

00:00:08.595 --> 00:00:09.971
- That's a great question, Katie.

00:00:09.971 --> 00:00:13.787
I think the reality would be if you live

00:00:13.787 --> 00:00:16.457
in a cosmopolitan city
like Toronto, New York,

00:00:16.457 --> 00:00:18.768
or near a city, you could actually go

00:00:18.768 --> 00:00:21.204
and there's tons of amazing communities,

00:00:21.204 --> 00:00:23.163
you know, there's massive
Cantonese communities,

00:00:23.163 --> 00:00:27.246
Mandarin community,
Indian community uhm...

00:00:27.246 --> 00:00:29.114
Bangladesh community and all these places.

00:00:29.114 --> 00:00:30.295
So, again, it depends.

00:00:30.295 --> 00:00:33.096
First of all, kind of
stick to what is your idea?

00:00:33.096 --> 00:00:33.929
What is your product?

00:00:33.929 --> 00:00:35.499
What is your mission?

00:00:35.499 --> 00:00:38.876
And then think about where is the audience

00:00:38.876 --> 00:00:40.879
that's going to be the
market for your product?

00:00:40.879 --> 00:00:42.631
Who are going to be your customers?

00:00:42.631 --> 00:00:45.596
And then, even, physically you might find

00:00:45.596 --> 00:00:48.910
that there's cities near you
where they're well-represented

00:00:48.910 --> 00:00:51.095
or the demographics are well represented.

00:00:51.095 --> 00:00:54.054
And then the next question,
if that's not the case,

00:00:54.054 --> 00:00:55.504
I don't know, say you you live

00:00:55.504 --> 00:00:58.671
in the middle of the Midwest in the U.S.,

00:00:58.671 --> 00:01:00.488
in a kind of rural community,

00:01:00.488 --> 00:01:03.100
then the great news is
the power of the internet

00:01:03.100 --> 00:01:05.505
has changed everything
in the last 20 years.

00:01:05.505 --> 00:01:08.419
So, you an go online,
you can find anything

00:01:08.419 --> 00:01:12.395
because you got an encyclopedia
at the palm of your hand,

00:01:12.395 --> 00:01:15.760
where you can find, and,
the other thing I have found

00:01:15.760 --> 00:01:17.538
some great entrepreneurs recently.

00:01:17.538 --> 00:01:20.289
They've just build a virtual business,

00:01:20.289 --> 00:01:22.111
of colleagues that met around the world

00:01:22.111 --> 00:01:23.962
through the internet.

00:01:23.962 --> 00:01:27.184
You know, there's actually
someone who's published a book,

00:01:27.184 --> 00:01:28.816
and they self-published it,

00:01:28.816 --> 00:01:33.792
and they actually got the
editor, I think, from Turkey.

00:01:33.792 --> 00:01:36.008
You know, they're out of New York state,

00:01:36.008 --> 00:01:37.138
but they got the guys,

00:01:37.138 --> 00:01:40.907
in terms of the
book-binding, out of Canada.

00:01:40.907 --> 00:01:43.249
So, you know, the world is a virtual world

00:01:43.249 --> 00:01:44.494
that's all there for you.

00:01:44.494 --> 00:01:46.399
And I think the opportunity,

00:01:46.399 --> 00:01:49.263
and actually this really helps
diversity and creativity,

00:01:49.263 --> 00:01:51.076
is there's tons of resources

00:01:51.076 --> 00:01:52.656
and brilliant people around the world.

00:01:52.656 --> 00:01:53.614
What, there's seven billion people,

00:01:53.614 --> 00:01:54.913
but there's a lot of people

00:01:54.913 --> 00:01:56.998
who want to support your success,

00:01:56.998 --> 00:02:00.307
or your idea, who are untapped resources.

00:02:00.307 --> 00:02:03.515
And they can either, even be mentors

00:02:03.515 --> 00:02:05.875
to you to help you on your journey

00:02:05.875 --> 00:02:07.217
and through social media,

00:02:07.217 --> 00:02:10.057
there's a great way of
connecting with them also.

00:02:10.057 --> 00:02:12.123
And the nice thing about,
you know, social media is

00:02:12.123 --> 00:02:14.659
there's almost a bond of trust.

00:02:14.659 --> 00:02:16.137
It's almost like, when we meet people,

00:02:16.137 --> 00:02:17.741
we have to get to know them,

00:02:17.741 --> 00:02:18.910
but with social media,

00:02:18.910 --> 00:02:21.722
you kind of meet someone
socially (laughs),

00:02:21.722 --> 00:02:23.610
and you automatically trust them.

00:02:23.610 --> 00:02:25.542
And if they have got something

00:02:25.542 --> 00:02:27.967
that helps your idea come to market,

00:02:27.967 --> 00:02:30.817
then why not, it's worth
testing that and pursuing that.

00:02:30.817 --> 00:02:32.502
And you actually can build a business

00:02:32.502 --> 00:02:34.512
and you can educate yourself, Katie,

00:02:34.512 --> 00:02:38.144
I think, very clearly around
where is your audience?

00:02:38.144 --> 00:02:39.140
Where is your market?

00:02:39.140 --> 00:02:41.706
And who is the network
of people I need to do

00:02:41.706 --> 00:02:45.873
to make that idea come to
reality and build a business?

00:02:46.858 --> 00:02:49.166
And it's all available through social,

00:02:49.166 --> 00:02:50.909
and it's all available
through the internet,

00:02:50.909 --> 00:02:52.979
So, we're really encouraged

00:02:52.979 --> 00:02:54.379
and obviously are really (mumbles)

00:02:54.379 --> 00:02:56.069
about coming on this show.

00:02:56.069 --> 00:02:59.162
There's probably loads of
people who are listening now,

00:02:59.162 --> 00:03:03.329
talking, paying questions and
who could be really powerful

00:03:04.892 --> 00:03:08.234
in your network to help
your idea come to market.

00:03:08.234 --> 00:03:11.251
- Listen, Katie, I think this
is part of entrepreneurship.

00:03:11.251 --> 00:03:13.400
You never have all the resources you want

00:03:13.400 --> 00:03:14.645
to do the thing that you want to do.

00:03:14.645 --> 00:03:17.209
You've got to find another
way to get started, right.

00:03:17.209 --> 00:03:20.011
Don't let the fact that you
don't have the money to travel

00:03:20.011 --> 00:03:21.376
be the reason why you don't go out

00:03:21.376 --> 00:03:23.309
and try to expand your mind, right?

00:03:23.309 --> 00:03:27.158
And I don't have a building,
so I can't, you know?

00:03:27.158 --> 00:03:28.177
We're always going to have these reasons

00:03:28.177 --> 00:03:29.702
why we can't do the things.

00:03:29.702 --> 00:03:32.026
Entrepreneurship's about
resourcefulness and finding a way.

00:03:32.026 --> 00:03:34.803
So what can you do in your
local city to find a way?

00:03:34.803 --> 00:03:37.741
Maybe there's meet-up groups, you know?

00:03:37.741 --> 00:03:39.439
There's salsa classes here in Toronto.

00:03:39.439 --> 00:03:41.699
I don't have to go to a different country

00:03:41.699 --> 00:03:43.658
to learn how to dance salsa.

00:03:43.658 --> 00:03:45.523
There's different activities
you can do around.

00:03:45.523 --> 00:03:47.027
There's different videos you can watch.

00:03:47.027 --> 00:03:49.448
I learn a ton from my own videos,

00:03:49.448 --> 00:03:50.281
where we cover,

00:03:50.281 --> 00:03:52.105
you guys give us suggestions
on videos, people to cover.

00:03:52.105 --> 00:03:56.189
People I've never heard of,
who have had massive success

00:03:56.189 --> 00:03:58.397
in countries outside of North America.

00:03:58.397 --> 00:04:00.153
I get to learn from that.

00:04:00.153 --> 00:04:01.913
And so, it's just finding a way.

00:04:01.913 --> 00:04:02.784
What do you want to learn?

00:04:02.784 --> 00:04:03.617
What are the skills?

00:04:03.617 --> 00:04:06.771
What are the people you want
to be able to connect with?

00:04:06.771 --> 00:04:08.007
There's probably a local group

00:04:08.007 --> 00:04:09.920
already covering that in some way,

00:04:09.920 --> 00:04:11.586
and if not, there's definitely one online

00:04:11.586 --> 00:04:12.615
that you can get involved with.

00:04:12.615 --> 00:04:14.810
So, much more, just
about the resourcefulness

00:04:14.810 --> 00:04:16.678
than the lack of resources.

00:04:16.678 --> 00:04:19.177
(plane taking off)

